\viewkind4\uc1\pard\cf1\lang1033\b\f0\fs36 Project Proposal: Community Issue Reporting and Management System\par
\b0\fs24\par
\b\fs28 1. Introduction\b0\fs24\par
The Community Issue Reporting and Management System is a web-based platform designed to bridge the communication gap between city residents and local municipal administrators. The application allows citizens to report infrastructure problems (such as road damage or lighting failures) and enables officials to track and resolve these issues systematically.\par
\par
\b\fs28 2. Objectives\b0\fs24\par
The primary objectives of the project include:\par
- Providing a user-friendly interface for residents to submit detailed issue reports with location data.\par
- Implementing a community voting system to help administrators prioritize high-impact issues.\par
- Creating a secure dashboard for administrators to manage categories and update issue statuses.\par
- Maintaining a transparent audit trail of all status updates and administrative notes.\par
\par
\b\fs28 3. Scope of Work\b0\fs24\par
The system consists of two primary user roles:\par
- \b Residents\b0 : Can register, browse existing issues, submit new reports in various categories, and vote on reports submitted by others.\par
- \b Administrators\b0 : Can manage the issue lifecycle, create new reporting categories, provide technical notes on repairs, and monitor system activity.\par
\par
\b\fs28 4. Technical Architecture\b0\fs24\par
The application is built using modern web development standards to ensure scalability and reliability:\par
- \b Backend Framework\b0 : Flask (Python) for robust server-side logic.\par
- \b Database Architecture\b0 :\par
  - Development: Local MySQL for prototyping.\par
  - Production: Neon Serverless PostgreSQL for high availability.\par
- \b Authentication\b0 : Flask-Login for secure session management and role-based access control.\par
- \b Styling\b0 : Vanilla CSS for a custom, professional UI design.\par
- \b Deployment\b0 : Hosted on Vercel with integrated CI/CD and cloud database storage.\par
\par
\b\fs28 5. Implementation Methodology\b0\fs24\par
The project followed a structured database-first approach:\par
- \b Conceptual Design\b0 : Creation of an Entity-Relationship Diagram (ERD) focusing on academic Notation (Chen's Style).\par
- \b Logical Design\b0 : Development of a Relational Schema (Grid Model) to map entities into physical tables.\par
- \b Data Migration\b0 : Development of custom scripts to synchronize data between local and cloud environments.\par
\par
\b\fs28 6. Conclusion\b0\fs24\par
The Community Issue Reporting System provides a transparent and efficient solution for municipal management. By combining resident engagement with administrative oversight, the platform ensures that public infrastructure issues are addressed in a timely and organized manner.\par
